#!/bin/bash
# Install Cisco's prebuilt OpenH264 so FreeRDP 3 can decode H.264 (RDP GFX
# AVC420/AVC444). Cisco's binary is the one covered by their MPEG LA patent
# license, so this repository downloads it instead of shipping it.
#
# Usage: freerdp3-install-openh264 [--remove]
set -euo pipefail

VERSION=2.7.0
SONAME=libopenh264.so.8
URL=https://ciscobinary.openh264.org/libopenh264-${VERSION}-linux64.8.so.bz2
SHA256=44ad0dd2c5af2bac84d26f89f2eb4e268708b8739323d15d33837f7221ce4980
DEST=/usr/lib64/openh264-cisco
CONF=/etc/ld.so.conf.d/openh264-cisco-x86_64.conf

if [ "$(id -u)" -ne 0 ]; then
	echo "Run as root." >&2
	exit 1
fi

if [ "${1:-}" = "--remove" ]; then
	rm -rf "$DEST" "$CONF"
	ldconfig
	echo "Removed Cisco OpenH264."
	exit 0
fi

if [ "$(uname -m)" != x86_64 ]; then
	echo "Only x86_64 is supported." >&2
	exit 1
fi

tmp=$(mktemp -d)
trap 'rm -rf "$tmp"' EXIT
echo "Downloading $URL"
curl -fsSL -o "$tmp/lib.bz2" "$URL"
echo "$SHA256  $tmp/lib.bz2" | sha256sum -c --quiet -
bunzip2 "$tmp/lib.bz2"

install -d -m 0755 "$DEST"
install -m 0755 "$tmp/lib" "$DEST/libopenh264.so.$VERSION"
ln -sf "libopenh264.so.$VERSION" "$DEST/$SONAME"
echo "$DEST" > "$CONF"
ldconfig
echo "Installed Cisco OpenH264 $VERSION to $DEST ($SONAME)."
echo "OpenH264 Video Codec provided by Cisco Systems, Inc."
